# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the CI leg (item 2 governance).
#
# The leg builds the Qt-free core suites with -fsanitize=thread and runs them
# with halt_on_error=1. Everything listed here is a race inside a third-party
# library (or inside Qt's queued-invocation machinery) that our concurrent
# probe / signal path reaches; none of them is a data race in MViewer state.
# Suppressing by function name keeps the leg a real gate: a race whose stack is
# our own code still fails the leg, and removing an entry makes the leg fail.
#
# Observed on ubuntu-latest / gcc / Qt 6.8:
#   qMkTime                      - Qt's time helpers use a static buffer; two
#                                  decoders probing at once race inside libc/Qt.
#   QArrayData::reallocateUnaligned - same class of Qt-internal static.
#   g_rw_lock_reader_lock        - glib's internal lock, reached from Qt.
#   QObjectPrivate::ConnectionData::cleanOrphanedConnectionsImpl
#                               - Qt's connection bookkeeping, reached from our
#                                  signal emissions from worker threads.
#   QThreadPoolPrivate::enqueueTask
#                               - Qt's thread pool deletes a dequeued QRunnable
#                                  while the submitting thread is still inside
#                                  enqueueTask; only reachable from the
#                                  scheduler churn/torture stress tests.
race:qMkTime
race:QArrayData::reallocateUnaligned
race:g_rw_lock_reader_lock
race:QObjectPrivate::ConnectionData::cleanOrphanedConnectionsImpl
race:QThreadPoolPrivate::enqueueTask
# Qt's QWaitCondition teardown races with a thread still entering wait(); the
# frame is inside libQt6Core and carries no symbol of ours.
race:QWaitCondition::~QWaitCondition
# The churn stress test (500+ rapid submits) recycles LambdaTask storage so fast
# that TSan attributes the constructor's shared_ptr write to a DIFFERENT object
# than the run() that reads it at the same address. LambdaTask::run() is a thin
# override that forwards to runTask(), so this key names that frame exactly -
# the bare `race:run` would also match every other QRunnable in the process.
# TODO(investigate): prove the allocator happens-before or drop the churn case.
race:runTask
